From 12ad40b7e7c003484f4a49aacd8d988e8edc1939 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 17:46:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] [DOSKUTSU] patch 0293 -- RUNMANIFEST schema-v2: real
 binary hash, fps decomposition + percentiles, pump-aware

The RUNMANIFEST block every QA cell emits was a well-designed skeleton left mostly
unpopulated, so the campaign was reconstructed by hand-written awk over per-frame
log lines. Populate it, and fix the one field that was actively misleading.

Provenance: binary_sha12 carried the compile-time -DDOSKUTSU_BUILD_SHA12 value, a
sha256-12 over the patch DIFF lines -- and by construction of scripts/org-cache.sh
that same value is ALSO the Organya PCM cache key. The field meant to prove "same
binary across rounds" reported the source/cache fingerprint under a name that says
binary. The real linked-binary sha256 is a post-link value unknowable at compile
time, and self-hashing a 7.75 MB exe at exit is too costly on a 486 and lands in
the #18/#32 quit window. So binary_sha12 now echoes the kit-verified 12-hex from a
DOSKUTSU.SHA sidecar (UNKNOWN when absent; binary_sha12_src records kit vs
unknown), while build_sha12 + organya_cache_key emit the source-diff value under
honest names.

fps decomposition emitted directly (previously hand-computed): fps_true_flips,
fps_true_render_s, reel_ticks, reel_game_seconds (DERIVED from ticks/50, not the
assumed 102), per_loop_fps, overhead_s -- all integer-counter derived, valid in
every cell including pump cells.

fps_p50/fps_p95 are REAL percentiles, computed at exit from the flip-probe's
inter_flip samples. Those samples already ship (the probe emits inter_flip_ms
every 10th flip, ungated -- the exact lines the campaign's awk parsed); Renderer.cpp
merely retains them into a bounded, lazily heap-allocated buffer (kept off .bss per
patch 0168-v2's TAS-determinism lesson), and this sorts them once. fps_p95 is the
reciprocal of the slow-tail (95th-pct) frame time -- the fps 95% of frames meet or
exceed, LOWER than fps_p50; fps_sample_n/interval label the decimation.

Pump awareness keys on the CLOCK, not the pump. With SDL/0122's MODE-2 timebase
active a gus/adlib cell's SDL clock is correct, so its percentiles are VALID;
INVALID_PUMP applies only when the pump ran with that fix off. CRUCIALLY the
timebase state is read from a RUN-TIME latch (g_timebase_was_active, set in the
flip path) rather than SDL_DOSOplTimerTimebaseActive() at emit -- that export is a
live ch0-ownership query and returns false post-SDL_Quit (pump stopped in
PumpStop), which would collapse the gate to _pump_active and mark every gus/adlib
cell invalid, the very data 0122 exists to rescue. pump_clock_state (no-pump /
pump-uncorrected / pump-timebase-ok) is derived from the same latch.

started_rtc_local (renamed from the misnamed started_utc): DOS has no timezone, so
the RTC is local wall time and no "Z" is emitted; a DOSKUTSU_RUN_UTC override is
honoured verbatim. duration_s stays an RTC interval, unaffected by a mis-set CMOS.
schema_version bumps to 2 (binary_sha12 changes meaning between corpora).

Block is open-coded via the header's exposed runmanifest_emit_kv_* helpers rather
than extending the shared include/runmanifest.h (co-owned with HWINV, out of lane).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
